class:: ScaleSpreadOsc
summary:: Continuously crossfaded oscillator bank distributed across a scale
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

ScaleSpreadOsc places a fixed number of oscillators across a scale stored as
frequency ratios. code::center:: moves the group and code::spread:: changes
the scale distance between adjacent voices. Fractional coordinates use
equal-power crossfades between neighboring degrees.

The scale buffer must be mono, contain at least two strictly ascending positive
ratios, and begin with exactly code::1::. The last entry must be below
code::period::. code::prepareScale:: performs the language-side checks and
loads the buffer.

Internally, every voice keeps a lower- and upper-degree phase, crossfades their
waveforms, optionally receives previous-sample modulation from its nearest
neighbor, and is distributed across stereo. The closest vanilla building block
is link::Classes/VOsc::. ScaleSpreadOsc differs by mapping a fixed oscillator
bank through arbitrary scale ratios rather than adjacent waveform buffers.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: bufnum
Number of a scale-ratio buffer prepared with code::prepareScale::.

argument:: freq
Signed root frequency in hertz.

argument:: center
Continuous scale coordinate at the center of the voice group. Negative values
wrap through lower periods.

argument:: spread
Distance in scale degrees between adjacent voices.

argument:: voices
Initialization-rate integer from code::1:: through code::32::. It remains
fixed for the life of the UGen.

argument:: period
Frequency ratio of one complete scale period. It must exceed the last stored
degree and is clamped no higher than code::16::.

argument:: modulation
Nearest-neighbor phase-modulation depth in radians.

argument:: stereo
Stereo distribution from code::0:: to code::1::. At code::0:: the returned
channels are identical.

argument:: waveform
Initialization-rate waveform: code::0:: sine, code::1:: triangle, or code::2::
saw.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied to both outputs.

argument:: add
Offset added to both outputs after multiplication.

returns::
A stereo array.

method:: prepareScale

argument:: server
The server that will own the buffer. The default is code::Server.default::.

argument:: ratios
A collection of at least two positive, finite, strictly ascending ratios whose
first value is code::1::.

argument:: action
Function passed to link::Classes/Buffer#*loadCollection:: after loading.

returns::
The allocated mono Buffer. Loading is asynchronous; call code::s.sync:: before
starting a Synth when using the return value directly.

method:: kr

ScaleSpreadOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

The UGen validates and remembers the buffer identity at construction. Freeing
or reallocating the buffer makes the instance silent and reports one server
error. Sine, triangle, and saw choices share the continuous scale mapping;
triangle and saw use bandlimiting helpers.

examples::

code::
(
Routine({
    var scale = ScaleSpreadOsc.prepareScale(
        s, [1, 9/8, 5/4, 4/3, 3/2, 5/3, 15/8]
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        ScaleSpreadOsc.ar(
            scale, 55, spread: 1, voices: 8
        ) * 0.06
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine({
    var scale = ScaleSpreadOsc.prepareScale(
        s, [1, 8/7, 4/3, 3/2, 7/4]
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        ScaleSpreadOsc.ar(
            scale, 48,
            center: LFNoise2.kr(0.15).range(-5, 5),
            spread: LFTri.kr(0.04).range(0.25, 2),
            voices: 12, period: 2,
            modulation: 0.15, stereo: 0.9,
            waveform: 1
        ) * 0.045
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

